      ]
    })} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(itemListSchema)} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "What is the best ecommerce platform for a small business in 2026?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Shopify is the best ecommerce platform for most small businesses in 2026 because the Starter plan at $39/month includes hosting, SSL, a payment gateway, and an app ecosystem that lets a solo founder launch a store in under an hour. WooCommerce is better if you already run WordPress and want full content control. BigCommerce is better if you want zero transaction fees at scale." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "Which ecommerce platform is cheapest for a new small business?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "WooCommerce is the cheapest ecommerce platform for a new small business because the plugin itself is free — you only pay for hosting ($10–$25/month), a domain ($12/year), and optional premium extensions. Wix eCommerce at $17/month is the cheapest all-in-one hosted option. Shopify Starter at $39/month is the best value when you factor in payment processing, SSL, and included apps." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "Is Shopify or WooCommerce better for a small business?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Shopify is better for small businesses that want a hosted, all-in-one platform with no server maintenance and a one-click app ecosystem. WooCommerce is better for small businesses that already use WordPress, want full ownership of their data, and need deep content marketing integration. For most non-technical founders, Shopify is faster to launch and easier to maintain." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "Can I switch ecommerce platforms later without losing data?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Most platforms support product CSV import/export, and Shopify, WooCommerce, and BigCommerce all offer migration tools or apps. Customer data and order history can usually be migrated, though URLs may change — plan for 301 redirects to preserve SEO. Starting on Shopify or WooCommerce makes future migration easier because both have mature export tooling." } }
      ]
    })} />
    <style>
      main { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #333; }
      h1 { color: #232f3e; font-size: 2rem; line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
      h2 { color: #232f3e; font-size: 1.5rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; scroll-margin-top: 80px; }
      h3 { color: #374151; font-size: 1.2rem; margin-top: 1.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
      .meta { color: #666; font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
      .toc { background: #f8f9fa; border: 1px solid #e5e7eb; border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; margin: 1.5rem 0; }
